  <h2 id="sales">Who pays for these skills, and how they judge you</h2>

  <p>
    Employers pay for skills that help the business, and clients pay for proven results. Both judge you by evidence of delivery.
  </p>
  <p>
    The first basic skill is writing a development goal that includes a date and a proof.
  </p>

  <h2 id="ai">AI and career planning and career development in organisations: which tasks are under pressure</h2>

  <p>
    AI tools help draft plans, suggest learning paths and summarise feedback. Generic plans sound alike.
  </p>
  <p>
    Honest self-review, relationships and evidence of results hold value. A staged path helps: now, use AI to draft and refine the plan; later, own the decisions and the conversations.
  </p>

